WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:01.530
It was quiet.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.910
Too quiet.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.390
That had been what everyone remembered about
that day.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:10.599
Ask any member of personnel who was working,
what was the one thing they recalled before…

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:11.610
it happened.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.910
They’d all tell you the same: that it had
been too quiet.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:22.630
An eerie lull in the Foundation’s usual
day-to-day activity, followed by untold, unspeakable

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.199
chaos.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:29.900
But the quiet had come first, and within that
quiet, a madman was hiding.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.059
His name was Vince Barrett, at least, that
was his legal name.

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:39.210
But he much preferred to go by his online
moniker of ‘TheTaintedLizard’, or just

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.300
‘The Zard’ for short.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.719
Anyone who chooses to call themselves something
like that in an attempt to sound cool might

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:52.449
well be a person to avoid, and in Vince – sorry,
The Zard’s – case, that sentiment was

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:53.449
accurate.

00:00:53.449 --> 00:00:57.840
He was a social recluse, devoting a lot of
his time to some of the darker corners of

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.789
the internet – and we don’t just mean
that he spent his days trawling through Reddit.

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:07.979
No, The Zard’s interests were in the paranormal,
the unusual and inexplicable, as well as the

00:01:07.979 --> 00:01:13.330
community of his fellow internet recluses
dedicated to unearthing the true supernatural

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.299
horrors of the world.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:19.710
Eventually, spending so much time in corners
of the online world where few normal people

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:24.670
would dare to tread, would lead to the Zard
becoming a member of the prolific forum known

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.670
as Parawatch.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:32.240
This was the real deal, not just urban legends
and blurry photos of Bigfoot, or faked handheld

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.040
videos of people falling into the Backrooms.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.900
Parawatch had long been known to, and kept
under the surveillance of, the SCP Foundation.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:41.900
Why?

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:47.159
Well, because this infamous online message
board would occasionally feature posts about

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:53.590
anomalies – some even including SCPs and
leaked information about the Foundation themselves.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:57.539
Of course, hardly any of these posts stayed
up for very long, before the Foundation’s

00:01:57.539 --> 00:01:59.430
tech teams scrubbed them permanently.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:05.400
But it was here, on the Parawatch forum, where
Vince Barrett would encounter a fateful video

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.400
clip.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.789
Acting fast, he managed to save the file before
it was taken down.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:14.990
It was footage taken from the bodycam of a
Foundation security officer, during the midst

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.739
of a containment breach.

00:02:16.739 --> 00:02:20.230
The Zard hit play, his hands shaking with
excitement.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.410
The original poster of the clip to Parawatch
had said that this footage was perhaps the

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:32.370
only video on the entire internet that depicted
something known as SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.910
Reptile.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:39.330
Of course, those familiar with 682 and the
SCP Foundation will need no introduction.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:44.060
But Vince, on the other hand, had only ever
heard rumors about the creature.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:49.750
And now, in the video playing on his computer
screen, he was seeing it for the first time.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.920
The Reptile was free from its containment
chamber, tearing its way through a Foundation

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.720
facility, and making quick work of dispatching
the security personnel that dared to stand

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.720
in its way.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:05.450
It was a force of unbridled carnage and rage,
destroying anything in its path and adapting

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.930
to its environment.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:11.739
Deep in the Parawatch forum, the Zard had
read rumors and leaks from alleged ex-Foundation

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:16.870
staff and detractors, that SCP-682 was like
something out of a nightmare.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:21.970
They’d said the creature could adapt perfectly
in response to damage inflicted upon it, or

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:26.790
to changes in its environment, as well as
heal any injury it sustained.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:33.330
It persisted, it kept on going, and something
about that enamored Vince to the infamous

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:34.490
anomaly.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:39.239
He thought it was beautiful, the ultimate
apex predator, and admired the hard to Destroy

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:40.989
Reptile’s tenacity…

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:43.099
as well as its ferocity.

00:03:43.099 --> 00:03:47.610
Watching the horrific containment breach footage,
he realized there and then that he was a devoted

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.890
fanatic of SCP-682.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:56.180
His time on the dark side of the web had twisted
his mind, and led him to make one fateful

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:00.390
decision: that he needed to see the creature
in person.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:04.930
That had been almost a year earlier, and in
the time since TheTaintedLizard had pulled

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.549
on every dark web string he knew of.

00:04:07.549 --> 00:04:12.659
Eventually getting in contact with a shady
group called the Chaos Insurgency, Vince had

00:04:12.659 --> 00:04:18.270
managed to get hold of a real-life SCP Foundation
key card, as well as the location of the facility

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:22.600
they were holding 682 in, and a forged transfer
document.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:27.900
Posing as a humble, unassuming janitor, The
Zard had made his way inside the Foundation,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:33.520
and wasted no time in making a beeline straight
for the acid tank where SCP-682 was held.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:38.320
He stared at the creature through the glass,
eyes wide and jaw slacked in utter awe of

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.280
the monstrous Reptile.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.830
Perhaps the biggest fan of SCP-682 on the
planet couldn’t quite believe he was standing

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.360
in the presence of the creature itself.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:52.139
It barely seemed to pay him any mind from
the other side of the tank, the acid surrounding

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:55.270
melting SCP-682 as fast as it could heal.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:59.880
Seeing it in containment enraged Vince; he
hated that the Foundation had kept what he

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:05.070
viewed as the perfect organism locked up,
after having tried time and time again to

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.070
destroy it.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.180
“Don’t worry,” the Zard murmured, approaching
the tank well over the minimum safe distance.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:15.020
“You’re a force of unparalleled destruction,
and you don’t deserve to be here.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.169
I’m going to set you free.”

00:05:17.169 --> 00:05:20.840
Unfortunately, after the glass had been smashed
and the alarms screamed out that another containment

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.449
breach was occurring, Vince would quickly
find out that the reptilian beast he revered

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:28.880
so highly didn’t quite hold him in the same
regard.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.930
If you thought the Zard was going to make
it all the way through this story alive, well,

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.630
then we regret to inform you that you’re
sorely mistaken.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:40.910
Although not as woefully misguided as Vince
himself, who was the first person in the path

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.120
of SCP-682 when he freed the creature.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.110
What all those leaks and rumors on Parawatch
had failed to mention about the Hard to Destroy

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:54.080
Reptile, was its vehement and relentless hatred
for all other forms of life… including its

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.139
very own fan.

00:05:56.139 --> 00:06:01.900
And TheTaintedLizard was only the first casualty
of SCP-682’s latest rampage.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.699
But this time was different.

00:06:03.699 --> 00:06:09.190
Sure, 682 was easily tearing its way through
SCP Foundation personnel left and right.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:13.259
Security teams were flung aside and ripped
to shreds as they tried in vain to re-contain

00:06:13.259 --> 00:06:14.270
the monster.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:18.300
Researcher staff found themselves tripping
over each other, trying to rush out of the

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:23.280
destructive path of the Hard to Destroy Reptile,
only to find themselves the next to face its

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.690
ferocious attack.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:32.169
In other words, it seemed to mostly be another
unbridled slaughter, common fare for an SCP-682

00:06:32.169 --> 00:06:33.169
containment breach.

00:06:33.169 --> 00:06:38.050
Except, rather than breaking its way out of
the facility, this particular instance saw

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:45.560
the creature heading in the direction of another
anomaly: SCP-914, better known as the Clockworks.

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:51.040
Now, if a rampaging regenerative reptile on
the loose wasn’t enough cause for concern,

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:56.240
then seeing it moving along its trajectory
to an anomalous refinement machine certainly

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.240
was.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:01.430
Those that had been on the other side of the
facility when the dearly departed Zard set

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:06.460
682 free, were now looking on in horror as
the Hard to Destroy Reptile burst into the

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.319
room housing SCP-914.

00:07:09.319 --> 00:07:14.509
The Foundation staff, in the midst of panic,
started at security monitors with bated breath,

00:07:14.509 --> 00:07:16.930
palpable fear hanging in the air.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:22.440
Each and every one of them knew that SCP-682
was more than just a mindless beast; the creature

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:27.010
was fiercely, frighteningly intelligent, sentient
even.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:31.090
And as it approached the controls for the
Clockworks, every onlooker secretly hoped

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:38.160
something or someone would step in at the
last second and prevent SCP-682 from entering

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.479
the machine.

00:07:39.479 --> 00:07:42.560
Unfortunately, that’s not what happened.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:49.400
SCP-914 whirred into life, its gears and gyros
spinning as SCP-682 entered the Input booth.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.169
Now, normally, the way the Clockworks operates
is by destroying any item placed within it

00:07:54.169 --> 00:07:57.180
and replacing it with something else in the
Output booth.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:01.400
Depending on its setting, it either completely
disintegrates an item, breaks down an object

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:05.800
into its base components, replaces it with
an equivalent or improves it.

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:12.240
And, being set to ‘Very Fine’ as it was
right now, SCP-914 can even add anomalous

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.129
properties to whatever is put in it.

00:08:15.129 --> 00:08:20.759
But what happens when an indestructible and
infinitely adaptable monstrosity is in the

00:08:20.759 --> 00:08:21.759
Clockworks?

00:08:21.759 --> 00:08:26.080
Well, it can’t destroy and recreate a better
version of something that’d known for being

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.530
Hard to Destroy… can it?

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:35.339
The entire machine was going haywire; SCP-682
was adapting to the refinement process, refusing

00:08:35.339 --> 00:08:41.720
to let SCP-914 unmake it, even to replace
it with an improved version of itself.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:46.630
The Hard to Destroy Reptile and the Clockworks
were at a momentary stalemate, watched with

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.730
bated breath by the Foundation.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:53.930
SCP-914 began to malfunction, its clockwork
components getting stuck as if the machine

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.190
was jammed.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:59.310
Its cogs were clogged up, unable to destroy
the subject in the Input booth.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:04.540
The room around was beginning to shake, in
fact, the very ground was trembling at the

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.790
force of the whole machine shuddering.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:11.041
“Enact the Abandon All Hope protocol,”
the Head of Research said desperately, watching

00:09:11.041 --> 00:09:13.730
the events unfold from the other side of the
building.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:18.060
The Site Director looked at them and nodded,
the pair of them entering their secure passcodes

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:21.110
to activate this secretive security measure.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:25.589
Just as they did, a small earthquake erupted
underfoot; the entire wing of the facility

00:09:25.589 --> 00:09:30.380
housing the Clockworks and SCP-682 had collapsed
into the ground.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:35.860
A huge crater was all that remained, littered
with wreckage of a whole portion of the Foundation

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:38.880
site, along with broken pieces of SCP-914.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:45.950
For the next few minutes, everyone was on
edge, secretly hoping that SCP-682 hadn’t

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:46.990
survived.

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:51.560
Maybe the Clockworks had managed to destroy
it, but the sheer force of doing so had caused

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.300
the machine to collapse in on itself.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:58.510
Or perhaps the hard to Destroy Reptile was
now buried beneath several thousand tons of

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:00.730
debris, dead at long last?

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:04.420
But the Foundation staff knew better than
to get their hopes up.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:09.010
And sure enough, just as an armed security
team approached the crater, something started

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:10.910
stirring in the rubble.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:16.970
Suddenly, SCP-682 came bursting out of the
crater, emerging in not quite the same state,

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:19.209
although no less deadly than before.

00:10:19.209 --> 00:10:23.250
The Clockworks hadn’t been able to unmake
the Hard to Destroy Reptile, but the resultant

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:28.320
malfunction and explosion had imbued the creature
with a whole host of new anomalous abilities.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:34.180
It still resembled its old self, but was now
more humanoid, standing bipedal instead of

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:36.070
on all fours.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:40.920
Some of its body mass had seemingly been reduced
due to damaged sustained in the malfunction,

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:45.740
although 682 was still plenty of feet taller
than any ordinary human being.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:49.260
In fact, it could be any height it needed
to be.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:54.450
The creature’s scaly skin seemed to be shifting
unnaturally, moving of its own accord, like

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:59.050
it was already preparing to adapt to oncoming
damage… and as the nearby security team

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:03.080
were about to find out, this made it even
deadlier than before.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:07.990
In a panic, the Foundation officers opened
fire, only to find that their weapons weren’t

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:10.019
operating the way they should.

00:11:10.019 --> 00:11:14.090
Something caused excitation of the copper
shells of their bullets, making them either

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:19.220
expand and block the barrels of their guns,
or causing them to backfire horribly, injuring

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.670
the security personnel wielding them.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:26.170
Before anybody could even call in air support
or heavy artillery as backup, a number of

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:31.540
the Foundation’s more powerful weapons suffered
even more catastrophic misfires.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:37.060
Missiles detonated early; they hadn’t even
been aimed at SCP-682 yet, but they would

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:38.060
have been.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:42.711
Instead, they exploded, taking with them a
huge number of Foundation casualties, some

00:11:42.711 --> 00:11:46.970
miles away from where the newly refined Reptile
now stood.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:52.639
SCP-682’s regenerative powers had been altered
by the Clockworks – it wasn’t purely reactive

00:11:52.639 --> 00:11:55.860
to oncoming damage now, it was pre-emptive.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.630
It could adapt to attacks that hadn’t even
happened yet.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:05.589
With no way of stopping it, SCP-682 began
decimating everything in its path with greater

00:12:05.589 --> 00:12:07.399
ferocity than ever.

00:12:07.399 --> 00:12:12.620
Over the coming days, the newly dubbed Impossible
to Destroy Reptile, began its biggest rampage

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:17.820
yet, entering a permanent rage state and unleashing
destruction on a global scale.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:22.770
It stormed through cities, and wiped out entire
major population centers in moments.

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:27.519
It seemed nothing on Earth could stand against
the refined reptile, fuelled by its singular

00:12:27.519 --> 00:12:31.410
mission: to wipe out all life in existence.

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:36.290
The surviving personnel of the SCP Foundation
soon came to learn that no damage could be

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.940
inflicted on the creature whatsoever.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:44.720
SCP-682 could predict attacks ahead of the
person that would carry it out, and then adapt,

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:49.079
changing the very world around it so that
attack never came.

00:12:49.079 --> 00:12:53.720
The Impossible to Destroy Reptile’s adaptations
usually took the form of diverting any oncoming

00:12:53.720 --> 00:13:00.290
damage it pre-empted it would take, and instead
inflicted that same damage on whoever it chose.

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:05.589
Even though the machine had malfunctioned,
the Clockworks had made SCP-682 that good

00:13:05.589 --> 00:13:11.260
at adapting to its surroundings that the creature
had almost become a universal constant.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:16.209
The fact it could not be harmed now seemed
to be as fundamental of a law as that of gravity.

00:13:16.209 --> 00:13:20.910
But that wasn’t going to stop the SCP Foundation
from trying.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:26.920
The number of casualties the world over had
been increasing steadily day by day as SCP-682

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:30.430
continued its devastating campaign of slaughter.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:34.670
Some of the remaining scraps of the Foundation
had tried to subdue the creature, but any

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:39.410
attempts at fighting it with conventional
weapons were ill-advised, to say the least.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:44.360
After all, how do you fight against a creature
that can predict your every move and counter

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:47.100
them before you’ve even thought of those
moves?

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:51.170
Well, you can try throwing something so unexpected
at it.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:57.199
At least, pulling something out of left field,
means the chances of SCP-682 seeing it coming

00:13:57.199 --> 00:13:58.350
are slightly slimmer.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:02.339
And that was where the Abandon All Hope protocol
came in.

00:14:02.339 --> 00:14:07.380
You see, the Foundation had been anticipating
that SCP-682 would one day become too powerful

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:12.690
to contain long before the creature had gained
its new ability to pre-emptively adapt.

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:16.600
And while the worldwide death toll had climbed
from hundreds of thousands of innocent people

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:20.990
to the earliest millions, an unlikely counterattack
was brewing.

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:25.850
One so unexpected that even the Impossible
to Destroy Reptile would struggle to see it

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:26.970
coming.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:31.670
Just as humanity was facing the brink of extinction,
the Foundation dispatched their last hope

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:36.589
at stopping SCP-682: other SCPs.

00:14:36.589 --> 00:14:40.820
The Abandon All Hope protocol had been devised
for when the suffering and destruction caused

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:46.470
by SCP-682 became so great that there was
no other option left.

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:51.339
When it had been activated, Foundation agents
stationed at various sites across the world

00:14:51.339 --> 00:14:54.830
had gathered a specially selected group of
anomalies.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:59.471
Each one was chosen because they were known
to be sympathetic towards humanity, or could

00:14:59.471 --> 00:15:03.860
at least be coerced into taking on SCP-682.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:08.949
And now, these SCPs were stepping up to the
plate, ready to fight the Impossible to Destroy

00:15:08.949 --> 00:15:13.680
Reptile… or more likely, to die trying.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:19.589
SCP-076-2, the immortal warrior known as Able,
was infamous for picking fights.

00:15:19.589 --> 00:15:24.560
The ancient Sumerian swordsman had a penchant
for seeking out the most challenging adversaries,

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:28.910
so convincing him to take a crack at SCP-682
wasn’t all that difficult.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:33.380
However, rushing into battle against the refined
reptile, Able quickly found he couldn’t

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:36.180
draw his weapons from his pocket dimension.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:40.540
They were dissipating the moment his fingers
touched them, vanishing faster than he could

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.540
draw them.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.800
No matter, the warrior thought; he’d been
alive for centuries, and had thus become a

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:48.829
master in every form of hand-to-hand combat.

00:15:48.829 --> 00:15:53.800
As you can imagine, he didn’t last very
long, left to slowly revive inside his stone

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:58.190
tomb after SCP-682 had finished dispatching
him.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:02.610
Able’s brother, Cain, incurred a slightly
different result when he went toe-to-toe with

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:04.700
the Impossible to Destroy Reptile.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:10.500
SCP-073 was hardly the fighter his brother
was, but had the anomalous trait of reflecting

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:14.310
incoming damage back at whoever was inflicting
it on him.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:19.490
So, when SCP-682 attacked Cain, theoretically
that same attack would have bounced back and

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:21.170
harmed the Reptile itself.

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:24.529
And before, that’s what would have happened.

00:16:24.529 --> 00:16:30.940
But now SCP-682 could adapt pre-emptively,
a strange never-before-seen phenomenon occurred.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:36.339
It appeared that neither SCP-073 nor the refined
reptile were harming each other at all.

00:16:36.339 --> 00:16:41.860
However, on a metaphysical level, the potential
damage of 682’s attacks against Cain were

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.700
being reflected back towards the Reptile.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:49.230
Only for the creature to pre-emptively adapt
to the damage from its own attack being inflicted

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:50.230
back.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:55.110
What resulted was a feedback loop of perpetual
possible damage that ended only when Cain

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.329
eventually passed out from shock.

00:16:57.329 --> 00:17:02.160
Unfortunately, while he could reflect damage
back at an attacker, he felt the pain of every

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.949
hit – and SCP-682 had more than just a mean
right hook.

00:17:06.949 --> 00:17:12.799
The Foundation had hoped, given its one hundred
percent mortality record, that SCP-096 would

00:17:12.799 --> 00:17:16.360
have no trouble killing the Impossible to
Destroy Reptile.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:20.280
Or at the very least, harming it enough so
that it could be subdued.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:26.289
After all, 682 still needed to see, and anyone
looking at the Shy Guy quickly met their end.

00:17:26.289 --> 00:17:32.230
But when the tall, pale humanoid approached
SCP-682, something unusual happened.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:37.580
The Reptile could look at SCP-096, able to
see it perfectly.

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:41.760
Perhaps the creature’s adaptive properties
were creating an intentional blind spot in

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:45.880
its vision, removing SCP-096 from view.

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:51.050
Or maybe SCP-682 no longer saw with just eyes,
perceiving the world in a manner far beyond

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.440
our understanding of basic sight.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:18:00.660
But whatever the case, the Impossible to Destroy
Reptile made SCP-096 turn and flee in terror.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:07.080
Compelled to put an end to the Reptile’s
reign of terror, SCP-4494, The Spectre, manifested

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.380
nearby and tried to intervene.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:14.580
The result was nothing short of brutal, a
one sided fight that not even the living embodiment

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:17.350
of crime fighting could hope to win.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:24.240
After SCP-682 had finished off the Spectre,
a strange, black fluid began oozing from nearby.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:27.789
Although one of the hardest to wrangle, the
Foundation believed that they had convinced

00:18:27.789 --> 00:18:32.830
SCP-106 to aid in taking down SCP-682.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:37.620
The Old Man emerged from the oily secretion,
shuffling menacingly towards the Impossible

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:39.090
to Destroy Reptile.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:44.669
It seemed to freeze, as if it was taking a
defensive stance against the Old Man… either

00:18:44.669 --> 00:18:47.960
that, or tricking him into getting closer.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:52.790
Before he could even reach out a decrepit
hand to touch the Reptile’s shifting skin,

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:58.340
SCP-106 was suddenly coated in copious amounts
of the black substance he secreted.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:04.120
It coated him like thick tar, the more his
decaying body produced, the more he was covered

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.120
in.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:09.150
Normally, he was resistant to the corrosive,
burning effect of this substance.

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:14.780
However, SCP-682’s pre-emptive adaption
powers had caused SCP-106 to overproduce the

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:20.980
oily substance; enough to rapidly dissolve
the Old Man into a steaming black puddle.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:27.270
It was at this point that SCP-343, colloquially
known as God, lowered his newspaper and looked

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:28.559
out of his window.

00:19:28.559 --> 00:19:32.409
That is to say, he looked out of the huge
hole that had been left in the wall of his

00:19:32.409 --> 00:19:33.409
cell.

00:19:33.409 --> 00:19:39.500
Being omniscient, SCP-343 was already burdened
with the awareness of what had happened; SCP-682

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:43.430
had been refined into an even worse version
of itself by the Clockworks.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:47.840
Up until now, God had been happy to avoid
all the fighting and just see how everything

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:54.190
worked out, but as much as he tried to distract
himself, SCP-682 slaughtering other SCPs in

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:56.470
droves was getting in the way of his reading.

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:59.179
“Ugh, this again,” God sighed, snapping
his fingers.

00:19:59.179 --> 00:20:04.010
In a split second, the entire universe had
been unmade and then remade almost exactly

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.140
the same.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:11.390
Except, SCP-343 had made a slight adjustment,
giving a little nudge to cause and effect

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.090
in a few places.

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:18.740
As a result, a certain misguided forum user
had never, and would never, infiltrate the

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:24.909
Foundation and break SCP-682 free, leading
to the Hard to Destroy Reptile being refined

00:20:24.909 --> 00:20:25.909
by the Clockworks.

00:20:25.909 --> 00:20:30.540
Although, while it had been unceremoniously
returned to its original form and placed back

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:37.000
in its acid tank, SCP-682 could still remember
the power it had wielded only moments before

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.059
everything had been rewritten.

00:20:39.059 --> 00:20:43.080
All it needed was another chance to get into
the Clockworks…

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:48.910
Now go check out “SCP-682 CRAZIEST MUTATIONS
AND ADAPTATIONS”! and “WHAT IF THE FLESH

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:50.920
THAT HATES WAS PUT INSIDE SCP-914?”

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.070
for more mutational craziness!

